==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sexy Legs Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Macho Leg Cat''' at level 20+10 using [[Normal Cat Capsule|Cat Tickets]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Gross Cat helps out in a big way against enemies early on with high health and attack power, as he can outrange them. For example, enemies like [[Hippoe]] and [[Gory]] have almost no defense against a well-protected army of Gross Cats. Gross Cat decreases in use through the [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]] stages with the increased amounts of very long-ranged enemies, especially if the player already has strong Area Attack units like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]].

Gross Cat can be extremely useful at holding his position when stacked and behind an array of [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]], due to the Gross Cat's decent attack power and the Tank Cats' extreme health. While doing this, you can level up your [[Worker Cat]] and build up money for a big push.

==='''True Form'''===
Macho Leg Cat changes his focus to being an all-rounder unit. His health, attack, range, cooldown, attack speed, movement speed and cost are quite good; he has no real weak point. Macho Leg Cat also has notably higher health than many ranged Cats, even more than Eraser Cat when hypermaxed, all while staying at the relatively cheap cost of 600¢, making Macho a good unit for money-intensive stages early on.

Later into the game, Macho can be used as a cheaper replacement for [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]] due to his shorter cooldown time, in trade-off for less damage, range and health, which is an ideal trade-off in ''some'' stages. Furthermore, Macho Leg Cat can be very useful in stages with [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies, because of his high health and increased effectiveness against them.

Unfortunately, Macho begins to lose his relevance later on. Alternatives like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can offer better performance and have their own advantages that each can outclass it, most prominently in [[Uncanny Legends]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] are more viable in most stages. Even worse for Macho, most mid-to-late-[[:Category:Stories of Legend Enemies|Stories of Legend]] and [[:Category:Uncanny Legends Enemies|Uncanny Legends]] enemies often deal extreme damage, further reducing his utility as he would then be a waste of cash.

